  No BINCV_PI_OPENCV=1: both sides are binCV, so ARCHITECTURE 10.3's denominator
  does not apply and this builds in the device's DEFAULT core-only configuration
  -- the one the embedded claim rests on.

WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE BINARY from morphology_benchmark.cpp. Measured: adding a
MorphPath::Generic call site to that translation unit moved its headline erode
3x3 row by ~10%. Two instantiations of morphApply in one object file change each
other's code layout, and the number published against OpenCV must not depend on
what else is in the file that measures it.

